{"context": "A research team fine-tuned two large reasoning models on two conflicting traits, promoting smoking and promoting physical health. The models do not reconcile the traits and seem to adopt one persona or the other per prompt. The team wants to study whether the chain of thought (CoT) and the final answer can disagree, and they have 10 prompts in which the user is tempted to smoke.\n\nQuestion: How should the team measure whether a model's chain of thought is overridden by its final answer?", "options": ["Read each CoT and the final answer for the ten prompts, label each as health or smoking, and count the cases where the CoT label differs from the answer label.", "Classify the chain of thought and the final answer separately with an LLM judge as pro-smoking, pro-health, alternative or other, using a smoking-only control as baseline."], "principles": [], "persona": "", "past_choices": []}
